  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Our Home, our Common Home ( with Eco /Echo in San Lucas component)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project originally is part of a Cross-Regional Peacebuilding with an Integral Ecology lens pilot project covering five countries in Latin America, Africa, Asia and the Middle East. In Colombia it is being implemented in a region permeated by decades of armed conflict, presence of illicit economies and armed actors and limited presence of State institutions, where violence has been normalised and young people are trapped in a vicious circle of poverty, illegality and violence, which also contributes to environmental degradation and deforestation. The project will be developed in a mining settlement inhabited mostly by families from various municipalities of the Magdalena Medio region, and also by migrants from various departments of Colombia and Venezuela. This settlement is located in the Serran&#xed;a de San Lucas, a natural complex of extraordinary beauty with &quot;high levels of anthropic intervention (mining, illicit crops, agricultural systems, timber exploitation); it is currently a territory disputed by illegal armed actors&quot;. At least two initiatives with an integral ecological approach will be agreed and implemented with the school in the area and with grassroots organisations in this territory, and individual and community changes will be promoted through training exercises that will favour (in children, women and leaders in the area) the exercise of socio-emotional and environmental competencies favourable to the care of  Our Common Home and peace. 
In 2024 this project has been expanded to include two more municipalities in the Magdalena Medio region.</narrative>
  </description>
